          "open_space_designation": "Metropolitan Open Land",
          "description": "The Property itself consists of a plot of land which formerly had a single tennis court on it and now is just derelict land with some metal storage containers housed at the Weigall Road frontage. The land is completely privately owned and is completely self-contained and fenced with padlocked gates and there are no public rights of access or rights of way across it. The former use as a single tennis court was not a public amenity but was an entirely private use and the current designation of the land as Metropolitan Open Land (MOL) is not feasibly within the accepted definition of Metropolitan Open Land. The proposed Development seeks to replace one currently disused tennis court, which would not be accessible to members of the public, with four high quality residential houses. ",
